Subject: dlm_slot: the trampolines' hold is volatile across the longjmp

xcall() and dlm_cdev_open() set h.m after DLM_SETJMP and read it on the
longjmp path to drop the hold.  ISO C leaves a non-volatile automatic
modified after setjmp indeterminate after the longjmp; the one-member
struct kept it in memory under GCC 2.7.2.3, but a compiler that splits
aggregates into registers (GCC 15 at -O, the host test build) reads a
stale value, so the hold leaks and the state harness fails three checks.
Declaring h volatile makes the code right for any compiler; the kernel
build's code is unchanged in effect (h.m already lived in memory).

--- a/dlm_slot.c
+++ b/dlm_slot.c
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@
 	long *a;
 {
 	struct dlm_guard g;
-	struct { struct dlm_mod *m; } h;	/* in memory: read after a longjmp */
+	volatile struct { struct dlm_mod *m; } h;	/* read after a longjmp */
 	label_t save;
 	struct dlm_mod *m;
 	int e;
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@
 {
 	struct dlm_cslot *cs = cslot((int)getmajor(*devp));
 	struct dlm_guard g;
-	struct { struct dlm_mod *m; } h;	/* in memory: read after a longjmp */
+	volatile struct { struct dlm_mod *m; } h;	/* read after a longjmp */
 	label_t save;
 	struct dlm_mod *m;
 	long a[8];
